MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_001: Hey, Simon! Been looking for you. Need a favor, if\nthat's alright.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_002: A favor? It's Mikaela, right? What could a guy like\nme offer someone as famous as you?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_003: Me? What about you? Sky-Drum Simon. That's the\nkinda nickname that puts fear in people's hearts!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_004: We'll be counting on each other, so I figured a\nsparring match would be a good idea.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_005: I'm trying to sharpen my skills up. With your\nreputation, you seem like a good whetstone.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_006: Sorry, but you're gonna have to ask someone else.\nI'm not really in the mood.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_007: You kidding? There's no such thing as too\nmuch practice.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_008: I'm warning you—if you hold back on me, we're just\ngoing to go again. Come on, time's wasting!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_009: I just said I'm not— Damn, she doesn't hear a word\nI say, does she?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_010: Whew... Not...bad! Was that a workout! I knew you\nwere the one to ask.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_011: You were incredible at reading my moves. I only\ntagged you at the very end!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_012: Your movements are slow. It's obvious where your\nattacks are coming from.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_013: You've let yourself go—which is a shame! I hear\nyou used to be something to behold.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_014: That right? You might be the best of the best, but\nyour attitude has some room for improvement.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_015: That said, you gave me a real fight even though you\ndidn't want to, so I can't complain.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_016: I look forward to next time. I'll see you around—\ncount on it.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_017: Hey, hey! Don't just assume I'll go along with your—\nDamn it... She never listens.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_018: Ugh. She may have only landed the one hit, but...\nI'll be feeling it later.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_019: Even with the rust, she's still Mikaela Redblade.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_020: What happened to the woman I met all those\nyears ago?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_C_021: I guess we've both changed since last we saw each\nother—not that she remembers me...
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_001: Whew. I really thought today would be the day.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_002: I've got my speed back, so I figured you couldn't read\nme. Guess I was wrong.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_003: I don't need to follow you with my eyes. After all\nthis time together, I know how you move.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_004: But you're doing well! Most people wouldn't dare\nto start training again at your age.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_005: Heh.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_006: Hey. Are you ignoring me again?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_007: I'm listening, alright. I was just thinking about the\nold days. You haven't changed.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_008: Here I am, coming to you. The roles have reversed,\nbut the script is the same.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_009: Wha— So you do remember! I was only 14 when\nyou were there!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_010: You thought I'd forget? If it wasn't for back then,\nI'd never have asked you to spar.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_011: Usually I steer clear of men like you—the ones who\ncan't keep it in their breeches.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_012: Well, when you say it like that, it sounds awful!\nI don't deny it though.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_013: Like I said, your reputation precedes you. Why mince\nwords? I am proud, though, to see you so strong.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_014: Funny that you're proud, considering you never\ntaught me anything.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_015: All you did was beat me up—an idiot kid.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_016: You just kept saying you'd "knock that rotten\nattitude" outta me.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_017: To be fair, you brought it on yourself. You had your\nhand in my purse!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_018: See, you really should thank me. I could have\nturned you in. Instead, I helped you out.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_019: "If you want the money, try and take it." Like a kid\nhad any chance against a grown mercenary...
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_020: That so? Well, now's your chance to turn the tables,\nso stop whining.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_B_021: Bold words considering how much I'm holding back.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_001: Is that a joke? I'll show you what's what!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_002: Impressive work, mopping up the leftovers. You seem\nto be as strong as you ever were, if not stronger.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_003: In terms of pure strength...maybe. I kept up my\ntraining during retirement.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_004: And sparring with me helped you draw out strength\nyou didn't know you had? Amazing work.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_005: Wow, the compliments come easy today. You must\nbe plotting something.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_006: No, nothing like that. I think the progress you've\nmade is incredible. Truly.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_007: To be honest with you, ever since I left home,\nI've felt...stuck.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_008: Well, maybe not stuck exactly. I've been free to do as\nI please, but...I haven't made any kind of progress.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_009: So today you're a warrior-slash-philosopher. OK.\nReally, though... What's the problem?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_010: Doing as you please? Clorisa would be happy to\nhear that.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_011: Hm? What does she have to do with this?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_012: Well, one time when you were knocked clean out,\nshe came and talked to me.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_013: She was worried. She thought that having to fight\nto protect the village, and her, weighed you down.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_014: Why haven't I heard this before?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_015: Well, it's not like she could tell you to just drop\neverything and be free, could she?
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_016: But what she did do was scrape together some of her\nsavings and hire me.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_017: I think what she really wanted was for me to give\nyou a push to move forward.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_018: She knew this was all she could do for you. She\nsmiled when she asked me, but she looked sad.
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_019: Clorisa...
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_020: So here I am. It's time for that push, big guy. Square\nin the back, full strength!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_021: That can't be what she meant! You'll break my spine\nif you go that hard!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_022: Ha! If you don't like it, all you have to do is stop\nme, right? Don't lose your nerve now!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_023: You may be a dog, but I enjoy having you as an\napprentice. You'll never be rid of me!
MID_SE_Mic_Sim_A_024: Heh. You're about the only person I'd let say that\nto me. You know that, right?